{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <functional>\n\nusing namespace std;\nusing i128 = __int128_t;\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nstruct UnionFind {\n    vector<int> data;\n    UnionFind(int n) : data(n, -1) {}\n    int find(int x) {\n        if (data[x] < 0) return x;\n        return data[x] = find(data[x]);\n    }\n    void unite(int x, int y) {\n        x = find(x); y = find(y);\n        if (x == y) return;\n        if (data[x] > data[y]) swap(x, y);\n        data[x] += data[y];\n        data[y] = x;\n    }\n};\n\nlong long count_cycles(long long p, long long k) {\n    UnionFind uf(p);\n    for (long long i = 1; i < p; ++i) {\n        long long next = (k * i) % p;\n        uf.unite(i, next);\n    }\n    vector<bool> seen(p, false);\n    long long res = 0;\n    for (long long i = 1; i < p; ++i) {\n        long long r = uf.find(i);\n        if (!seen[r]) {\n            seen[r] = true;\n            ++res;\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nlong long solve(long long p, long long k) {\n    long long cycles;\n    if (k == 0LL) cycles = p - 1;\n    else if (k == 1LL) cycles = p;\n    else cycles = count_cycles(p, k);\n    \n    long long ans = 1;\n    for (long long i = 0; i < cycles; ++i) {\n        ans = (ans * p) % MOD;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    cout << solve(p, k) << endl;\n    int dummy;\n    cin >> dummy;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nMOD = 1000000007\n\nclass UnionFind:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.data = [-1] * n\n    \n    def find(self, x):\n        if self.data[x] < 0:\n            return x\n        self.data[x] = self.find(self.data[x])\n        return self.data[x]\n    \n    def unite(self, x, y):\n        x = self.find(x)\n        y = self.find(y)\n        if x == y:\n            return\n        if self.data[x] > self.data[y]:\n            x, y = y, x\n        self.data[x] += self.data[y]\n        self.data[y] = x\n\ndef count_cycles(p, k):\n    uf = UnionFind(p)\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        next_val = (k * i) % p\n        uf.unite(i, next_val)\n    \n    seen = [False] * p\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(1, p):\n        r = uf.find(i)\n        if not seen[r]:\n            seen[r] = True\n            res += 1\n    return res\n\ndef solve(p, k):\n    if k == 0:\n        cycles = p - 1\n    elif k == 1:\n        cycles = p\n    else:\n        cycles = count_cycles(p, k)\n    \n    ans = 1\n    for i in range(cycles):\n        ans = (ans * p) % MOD\n    return ans\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    p, k = map(int, input().split())\n    print(solve(p, k))\n    dummy = int(input())\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001479277852922678, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.20340192317962646, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.003181398380547762, 0.0, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, 0